# direnv. This file carries CCT_BOT_TOKEN, so it is a credential slot by
# design even on the days its value happens to be indirected. Ignored for
# the same reason claude-code-telegrammer ignores its own .envrc: the risk
# is not what the file holds today, it is that a literal lands in it later
# and nothing is watching. sac now resolves the bot token from the fleet
# pool (CCT_BOT_TOKEN_<SLOT> via SAC_SECRETS_ENVRC), so a per-project
# .envrc is machine-local convenience, not shared configuration.
.envrc
